  "_notes": [
    "The O'Connell ground truth: the position log read BY HAND off the pixels.",
    "",
    "It exists because the reader is right about the STRUCTURE and has to be",
    "MEASURED about the values. The corpus's position logs are screenshots at",
    "five different resolutions (1342x437, 1378x527, 1844x578, 1973x765 and",
    "2085x729), and the same cell is 60 pixels wide in one capture and 90 in",
    "another. A reader that is right on one resolution can be wrong on another,",
    "and a number that is not measured is a number nobody can argue with.",
    "",
    "Every entry below was read off the image by eye, field by field, and the",
    "test asserts the reader reproduces it. Where the reader cannot, the",
    "difference is recorded here rather than hidden.",
    "",
    "A LOT is one row of the position log. The same ticker is on several rows",
    "when it was bought several times, so a lot is keyed by its ticker, its",
    "contract, its entry date and its cost basis."
  ],
